00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.990
So, Borka wants to talk to me?!

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:48.650
Borka's robbers had selfishly moved into the north side of the Mattis' castle without asking

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:54.250
Mattis and his robbers rushed to Hell's Gap to kick them out right away,

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.850
but it didn't go as well as he had planned.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.680
Ronja then went into the forest to vent her pent-up feelings,

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.610
but there...

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.520
Song in the Fog

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.520
Song in the Fog

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.380
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.510
How much of a hurry I'm in has nothing to do with you!

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:13.150
I need to keep an eye on what that bad mouthed dirty devil is doing in my woods!

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:51.280
What do you want, robber's daughter?

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:04.740
Now I'm sure you're a dirty devil Borka robber.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.490
How dare you take my foxes without asking!

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:12.700
It's not just us who steal things without asking.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.370
Your father does that too, no?

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:18.960
Anyway!

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.380
Leave my fox cubs alone!

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:25.270
I want you to disappear from my woods!

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.670
Your fox cubs?! Your woods?!

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.800
Nobody <i>owns</i> fox cubs!

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.400
They belong to themselves!

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:53.940
And they live in a fox's wood.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.240
Not only that, this is the wolves', and bears', and elks',

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.670
and wild horses' wood too.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.170
The owls', and the hawks', and the cuckoos' wood.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:10.750
And the snails', and the spiders', and the ants' wood.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:15.930
I know all the living things in these woods.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.970
So don't think you have to teach me anything!

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:26.340
Then you know that it's also the wild harpies', and the gray dwarfs', and the rumphobs',

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:30.080
and the murktrolls' wood, right?

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.700
Tell me something I don't know.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:37.970
Something I don't know better than you.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:40.210
Otherwise, shut up.

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:44.420
In any case, it's my wood!

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.870
And your wood...

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:48.130
robber's daughter!

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:59.020
But if you want it for yourself alone,

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:05.810
then you are sillier than I thought when I first saw you.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:14.360
I'm happy to share the woods with the foxes, and owls, and spiders,

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:17.770
but not with you!

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.380
Ronja!

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:08.180
Ronja!

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:13.860
Ronja!

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:16.130
What do you want?!

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:25.560
This mist... scares me a little.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:28.740
I see!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:34.450
You're frightened of not getting to the home you stole for yourselves?

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.180
Then you'd better share the foxes' lair with them.

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:40.810
Because this is your woods.

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:43.250
And the foxes' as well, right?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:52.250
You're harder than stone, robber's daughter.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:58.310
But I guess you can find your way to the castle better than I can.{Mattis'}

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:03.770
May I hold on to the edge of your tunic until we're out of the woods?

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:20.050
Here. But you'd better keep a rope's length away from me.

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:22.210
I'm warning you...

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.700
As you'd like,

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.330
spiteful robber's daughter.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.150
All right.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:02.570
Are you lost?

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:04.480
This is the rock marker.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:05.800
We're going the right way.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:43.140
Why?

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.730
This means I've been walking in circles?

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:49.040
Hey!

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:11.200
It's okay.

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.140
I'll be home soon.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:17.130
And I'll listen my mother's lullaby.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:18.880
Birk.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:21.130
Birk!

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:26.550
Birk!

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.190
They are calling me...

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:31.580
Yes, I'm coming...

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:40.400
Ronja!

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:44.460
Where are you going?!

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:49.840
If you let yourself be tempted away by the unearthly ones, you'll be lost forever!

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:51.470
You know that, right?!

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:01.150
Yes, I'm coming!

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:03.980
Don't!

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:08.810
Let me go!

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.490
Let me go!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.820
Don't upset yourself!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.640
I'll go! Let me go!

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:28.200
Yes, I'm coming!

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.650
You shouldn't!

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:30.510
Let me go!

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:32.660
I'm telling you, let me go!

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:33.910
No!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:36.960
Let me go!

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:43.520
Let me go! Let me go!

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:46.630
Let me go!

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:50.860
Let me go!

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:53.260
Let me go...

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:56.600
Let me go...

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:35.900
A rope's length away I said!

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:41.250
Did the fox... bite you?

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.250
Thank you.

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:51.360
I'm okay now. I can find my own way home to Borka's keep.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:16:02.770
Ronja suddenly found it difficult to think really badly of him.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:08.060
She did not know why.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:12.800
People like you should be throw into Hell's Gap!

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:47.280
Lovis said tending to the sheep will take a bit longer than usual.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:52.480
Now that it's fall, the nights are cold.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:53.690
Daddy.

00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:59.200
What is it that you've taken without asking?

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:10.840
I was so afraid you wouldn't find your way back home in the fog.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.260
My Ronja.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.740
But I did.

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:22.140
Listen, what is it that you have taken without asking?

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:27.100
Well, it's...

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.330
Oh yes, a lot of things.

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:31.110
For example, my...

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:32.620
Stop that for now, old man.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:36.290
This is something I should deal with myself.

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:45.340
My Ronja, you are still an innocent child,

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:49.120
that's why I haven't talked much about it before.

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:51.130
Uh-huh.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:54.860
No, you haven't said a word.

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:58.170
And we weren't allowed to say anything either.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:03.060
Old man, isn't it about time you went to bed?

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.870
That won't happen.

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:06.990
By the devil himself,

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:11.780
I want to stay here and listen to everything.

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:17.030
Listen carefully, my Ronja.

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:19.520
Uh-huh.

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:35.710
So the stuff you guys brought back in the evenings was

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:39.660
stuff you took without asking from people who pass through the forest, right?

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:46.680
But I wonder if they get terribly angry when you take their things away from them...

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.810
Of course they get angry.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.780
Aah! Aah! So loud.

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:56.230
Ronja, you should just hear them.

00:18:56.720 --> 00:19:00.150
Old man, it would be a good thing if you finally went to bed now.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:02.700
And some of them even cry.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:03.860
Shut up!

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:07.090
Otherwise, I'll throw you out!

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:13.330
You've just got to understand,

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:16.380
that's just the way it is.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.660
This is the way it has always been.

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:21.760
It's nothing to make a fuss about.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:25.000
No, it really isn't.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:28.400
But people never do get used to things.

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:32.260
They go on howling, and crying, and swearing...

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:35.030
'Till it's a pleasure to hear them.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:43.740
As you know, my father, my grandfather, and my great-grandfather,

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.900
they were all robber chieftain.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:48.550
And I am one too.

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:53.110
I'm the mightiest robber chieftain in all the mountains or woods.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:58.210
And that's what you're going to be too,

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:00.840
Is that all right? My Ronja.

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:02.920
Never!

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:07.210
I won't be like that as long as I live!

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:12.020
If everyone gets angry and cries, I definitely won't be a robber!

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:22.920
Please understand, Ronja!

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:26.360
I take only from the rich!

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:29.890
I won't hurt them, and I of course won't take their lives!

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:33.540
And also, also...

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:34.730
Yes!

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:39.900
And I give to the poor, I really do!

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:42.590
Yes, that's true enough.

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:49.550
When was it... you gave that poor widow with the eight children a whole sack of flour, remember?

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:51.060
Yeah!

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:54.060
That must have been ten years ago.

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:59.780
Of course you give to the poor.

00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:03.450
Every ten years, occasionally.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.790
Hey, old man!

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:13.910
If you don't go to sleep now, I'm going to throw you into bed myself!

00:21:15.070 --> 00:21:17.250
What's all this noise?

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:40.860
Ronja, you should also head to bed.

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:56.640
<i>Wolves, Wolves</i>

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:56.640
<i>Wolves, Wolves</i>

00:21:56.640 --> 00:22:01.060
<i>Howl in the forest at night</i>

00:21:56.640 --> 00:22:01.060
<i>Howl in the forest at night</i>

00:21:57.050 --> 00:22:03.130
It really doesn't bother me if Daddy is the robber chieftain.

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:10.630
<i>They howl and wail because they can't sleep</i>

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:10.630
<i>They howl and wail because they can't sleep</i>

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:07.450
No matter what he is doing...

00:22:07.450 --> 00:22:10.630
He is still my treasured father.

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:19.930
<i>Their stomachs are empty</i>

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:19.930
<i>Their stomachs are empty</i>

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:18.660
